---
import { css } from 'styled-system/css'
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro'
import Callout from 'web-design-system/astro/marketing/Callout.astro'
import CodeBlock from 'web-design-system/astro/product/CodeBlock.astro'
import TableScroll from '../components/TableScroll.astro'

const toc = [
  { label: 'Prerequisites', href: '#prerequisites' },
  { label: 'Install Nix', href: '#install-nix' },
  { label: 'Install direnv', href: '#install-direnv' },
  { label: 'Enable nix-direnv', href: '#nix-direnv' },
  { label: 'Allow the environment', href: '#allow-the-environment' },
  { label: 'Run the app', href: '#run-the-app' },
  { label: 'Command reference', href: '#command-reference' },
  { label: 'Web surfaces', href: '#web-surfaces' },
  { label: 'Troubleshooting', href: '#troubleshooting' },
]

const installNix = `# Recommended: the Determinate Systems installer (flakes enabled by default)
curl -L https://install.determinate.systems/nix | sh -s -- install

# Or the official multi-user installer, then enable flakes in /etc/nix/nix.conf:
#   experimental-features = nix-command flakes
curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh -s -- --daemon`

const installDirenv = `nix profile install nixpkgs#direnv   # or: brew install direnv / apt install direnv

# Hook it into your shell (bash shown; see \`direnv hook --help\` for others)
echo 'eval "$(direnv hook bash)"' >> ~/.bashrc`

const nixDirenv = `git clone https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv ~/.config/direnv/nix-direnv
echo 'source ~/.config/direnv/nix-direnv/direnvrc' >> ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc`

const allowEnv = `# From the repository root
direnv allow

# The first run builds the devShell and takes a while; later shells load from
# the nix-direnv cache. Verify it worked:
direnv status        # should show "Found RC allowed true"
which cargo rustc    # should resolve into the Nix store`

const runApp = `cargo run -p todo-2    # run the desktop app
t2                     # or run it under cargo-watch for auto-rebuilds`

const commands = [
  { command: 'cargo run -p todo-2', purpose: 'Run the desktop app.' },
  { command: 't2', purpose: 'Run the desktop app under cargo-watch, rebuilding on change.' },
  { command: 't2-bundle', purpose: 'Assemble the macOS bundle (icon, Info.plist, signing) without launching it.' },
  { command: 'ccheck', purpose: 'cargo check the main workspace crates.' },
  { command: 'tt', purpose: 'Run the Rust test suite, with macOS codesign/quarantine fixups for the test binaries.' },
  { command: 'testdbg', purpose: 'Run the storage tests with debug logging.' },
  { command: 'mig <args>', purpose: 'Run a storage migration (cargo run --bin migrate -- migration ...).' },
  { command: 'clone-patch <crate>', purpose: "Clone a crate's upstream repository into patched/ to vendor a fork." },
  { command: 'skills', purpose: 'Sync docs/agent_skills/*.md into .agents/skills/.' },
  { command: 'web', purpose: 'Install the JS workspace, stop any dev server left by a previous session, and start the docs site.' },
  { command: 'dev-stop', purpose: 'Stop the dev servers the web packages left running.' },
  { command: 'astro <args>', purpose: "The workspace's pinned Astro CLI, e.g. astro dev status or astro check." },
  { command: 'pnpm dev', purpose: 'Run this documentation site with auto-rebuilds.' },
  { command: 'pnpm dev:ds', purpose: 'Run the design-system showcase with auto-rebuilds.' },
]

const webCommands = `pnpm install      # install the pnpm workspace (design system, showcase, docs)
pnpm dev          # this site (Astro's default port, or the next free one)
pnpm build:docs   # static build of this site
pnpm dev:ds       # the design-system showcase
pnpm typecheck    # typecheck all three JS packages
pnpm test         # Vitest suite for the design system
pnpm test:e2e     # Playwright smoke, theming, and WCAG 2.1 AA checks`
---

<Docs
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Get the repository running: Nix provides the toolchain, direnv loads it automatically, and cargo runs the desktop app."
  toc={toc}
>
  <Callout tone="note" title="Prerequisites">
    A Unix-like machine (macOS is the main target today; Linux works for the Rust crates), Nix with
    flakes enabled, and direnv. The dev shell also brings Node and pnpm for the web packages, so you do
    not need those installed globally.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
  <p>
    The repository uses <a href="https://nixos.org">Nix</a> flakes for its development environment: the
    <code>.envrc</code> file loads <code>flake.nix</code>, which provides the Rust toolchain,
    <code>cargo-watch</code>, Node, pnpm, and the helper commands used below. direnv with
    <a href="https://github.com/nix-community/nix-direnv">nix-direnv</a> loads it automatically when you
    <code>cd</code> into the repo and caches the shell between visits.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install-nix">Install Nix</h2>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={installNix} showLineNumbers={false} />
  <p>Open a new shell afterwards so <code>nix</code> is on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="install-direnv">Install direnv</h2>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={installDirenv} showLineNumbers={false} />

  <h2 id="nix-direnv">Enable nix-direnv</h2>
  <p>
    nix-direnv caches the built devShell, so re-entering the repository is fast. The manual install:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={nixDirenv} showLineNumbers={false} />
  <p>
    Alternatively, use the <code>nix-direnv</code> Home Manager or NixOS module.
  </p>

  <h2 id="allow-the-environment">Allow the environment</h2>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={allowEnv} showLineNumbers={false} />

  <h2 id="run-the-app">Run the app</h2>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={runApp} showLineNumbers={false} />
  <p>
    <code>t2</code> is the usual development loop: it runs the binary under <code>cargo-watch</code> so
    logs stream to the terminal and rebuilds happen on save.
  </p>

  <h2 id="command-reference">Command reference</h2>
  <p>The dev shell adds the following commands, all available from the repository root.</p>
  <TableScroll label="Dev shell commands">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>What it does</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          commands.map((entry) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{entry.command}</code></td>
              <td>{entry.purpose}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </TableScroll>

  <h2 id="web-surfaces">Web surfaces</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>pnpm</code> workspace holds three packages: the design system
    (<code>libs/web-design-system</code>), its showcase (<code>demos/design-system-showcase</code>), and
    this documentation site (<code>apps/docs-web</code>). None of them are Cargo members.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={webCommands} showLineNumbers={false} />
  <Callout tone="warning" title="Class parity">
    The design system, the showcase, and this site each run Panda codegen. Their <code>panda.config.ts</code>
    files must keep <code>hash</code>, <code>separator</code>, and <code>prefix</code> identical, and each
    app's <code>include</code> globs must cover the design system's source. If they drift, components render
    unstyled with no error.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>direnv reload</code> re-evaluates <code>.envrc</code> after a change (for example, <code>flake.lock</code>).</li>
    <li><code>direnv status</code> explains why the environment is or is not loaded.</li>
    <li>
      If builds fail on a fresh lockfile, try <code>direnv reload</code> or <code>nix flake update</code>
      in the repository.
    </li>
    <li>
      On macOS, launching a bundled <code>.app</code> can prompt for access to Documents/Music/Photos;
      running the raw binary under <code>t2</code> keeps the shell's existing permissions.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
